    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "Implements ADR-013 (docs/decisions/013-length-units.md).\n\n## Summary\n\nAdd px, em, rem, %, and auto (horizontal margins) support to layout. Today anything that is not Npx silently becomes 0, which is why example.com renders as a left-aligned box in our browser but centered in Firefox.\n\n## Scope\n\n1. LengthContext + parse_length in style_values.{hpp,cpp}. Replace parse_px. Add is_auto. Units: px, em, rem, %, auto.\n2. Remove font-size from kInheritedProperties in cascade.cpp. Ship together with item 3.\n3. Thread parent_font_size and root_font_size through layout_element. Compute own font-size first.\n4. Auto horizontal margin centering in layout.cpp.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- [ ] All four changes implemented\n- [ ] Unit tests for px, em, rem, %, auto\n- [ ] Font-size inheritance: html { font-size: 20px } p { font-size: 2rem } gives 40\n- [ ] p { width: 600px; margin: 0 auto } centers\n- [ ] p { padding: 1em } with 16px font-size gives padding 16\n- [ ] grep -rl \"lexbor/\" src/ returns only src/renderer/html/convert.cpp\n- [ ] CI green\n\n## Delivery in three stages (one commit)\n\n- Stage A: LengthContext, parse_length, is_auto, unit tests. No behavior change.\n- Stage B: cascade + layout font-size change (atomic).\n- Stage C: auto centering.\n\n## Deferred (per ADR-013)\n\nViewport units, ch/ex, absolute units, calc(), height %, auto for width/top/bottom margins.\n\n## Refs\n\n- ADR-013: docs/decisions/013-length-units.md\n- ADR-012: docs/decisions/012-shorthand-expansion.md\n",
